WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.768
The school assigns burns and hypothermia this week. Its listed provincial pages also include electrical contact and heat illness, so these are part of the reading rather than optional missing pages.
学校本周指定烧伤及低体温，列出的省级页面也包含电接触及热病。因此这些是阅读的一部分，不能作为可选页漏掉。

00:00:12.768 --> 00:00:26.448
A thermal burn needs cooling of the injury while preventing whole-body heat loss. A hypothermic patient needs protection and the appropriate rewarming plan. A heat-stroke patient needs rapid active cooling.
热烧伤需要冷却损伤，同时防止全身热丢失；低体温患者需要保护及适当复温；热射病患者则需要迅速主动降温。

00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:37.368
Do not combine these into a single temperature checklist. Identify the mechanism and current physiology, then predict the effect and possible harm of each intervention.
不能把它们拼成同一温度清单。应识别机制及当前生理，再预测各项干预的效果及可能伤害。

00:00:37.368 --> 00:00:49.896
The paired guides include every named Week Four BCEHS identifier and all thirteen BCPEG pages, with current-versus-school differences labelled. They are not a substitute for supervised device competence.
中英导读包括第4周全部BCEHS编号及十三页BCPEG，并标明当前与学校版本差异；它们不能替代监督下器械技能。

00:00:49.896 --> 00:01:00.264
A forty-eight-year-old walks toward the crew after hot liquid and a brief flame exposure. The right arm and anterior trunk are painful, and the patient is shivering.
一名48岁患者在热液及短暂火焰暴露后，自己走向团队。右臂及前躯干痛，并在发抖。

00:01:00.264 --> 00:01:10.632
There was also brief smoke exposure in an enclosed space and the voice is changing. Talking now does not guarantee that the airway will remain safe during transfer.
患者也曾短暂在封闭空间吸烟，声音正在改变。现在能说话，不保证转移中气道仍安全。

00:01:10.632 --> 00:01:22.176
Begin scene safety and the primary assessment, stop any continuing injury and assess for other trauma. The burn appearance must not distract from breathing or circulation.
应先评估现场安全及初级威胁，停止持续损伤，并寻找其他创伤。烧伤外观不能使你忽略呼吸或循环。

00:01:22.176 --> 00:01:32.760
Ask the injury time and what cooling has already been effective. That history informs further care; it is not a reason to restart the clock and cool indefinitely.
应询问受伤时间及此前哪些冷却有效。这有助决定后续照护，不是重开计时并无限冷却的理由。

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:45.384
A fire being out does not prove that the air, structure or electrical system is safe. Use the rescue and hazardous-zone plan rather than entering because you possess gloves or an oxygen cylinder.
火灭了，不证明空气、结构或电气系统安全。应使用救援及危险区域方案，不能因有手套或氧瓶就进入。

00:01:45.384 --> 00:01:58.392
Stop continuing heat exposure and extinguish burning material through the safe appropriate method. Remove nonadherent clothing and jewellery that retains heat or may become constrictive as swelling develops.
应以安全适当方法停止持续热暴露并灭掉燃烧物。移除不粘连且保热，或随水肿形成束缚的衣物及首饰。

00:01:58.392 --> 00:02:08.040
Do not pull melted clothing or adherent material off the wound. Protect the area and communicate what remains so the receiving team can manage it safely.
不能把融化衣物或粘连材料从伤口硬拉下来。应保护部位并交代残留，让接收团队安全处理。

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:18.720
Chemical and electrical sources need their own hazard control. A thermal-cooling routine does not replace power isolation or agent-appropriate decontamination.
化学及电源需要各自危险控制。热烧伤冷却常规不能替代断电隔离或适合化学品的去污。

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:30.576
Superficial epidermal injury is commonly red, dry and blanching. Partial-thickness injury extends into dermis and is often moist, blistered and painful.
表浅表皮伤常红、干且可压褪色。部分皮层伤进入真皮，常湿润、有水疱且疼痛。

00:02:30.576 --> 00:02:45.048
Deeper injury can be paler, drier, less blanching and less sensitive. Full thickness may be leathery, white, brown or charred, with an insensate centre and painful surrounding mixed injury.
更深损伤可较白、干、不易褪色及感觉低。全层可呈皮革样、白、棕或焦黑，中央无感觉而周围混合伤仍痛。

00:02:45.048 --> 00:02:57.384
Do not call a painless burn minor or rely on one feature to determine final depth. Describe the findings and the uncertainty; depth can evolve after the field examination.
不能把不痛烧伤叫轻伤，也不能靠一项特征判断最终深度。应描述发现及不确定，因为院前检查后深度还会变化。

00:02:57.384 --> 00:03:08.232
The immediate task is to recognize the significant injury and protect the patient. Do not delay essential care for a debate over the exact depth of every centimetre.
即时任务是识别重要损伤及保护患者。不能为了争论每厘米精确深度而延误关键照护。

00:03:08.232 --> 00:03:20.928
The adult rule of nines gives head and neck nine percent, each entire arm nine, each entire leg eighteen, the anterior trunk eighteen, posterior trunk eighteen and perineum one.
成人九分法为头颈9%、每条完整上肢9%、每条完整下肢18%、前躯干18%、后躯干18%，以及会阴1%。

00:03:20.928 --> 00:03:32.712
Those are whole regions. The front of an arm is not the entire arm, and two sides must not be accidentally counted twice. Estimate the burned fraction of each region.
这些是完整区域。上肢前面不等于整条上肢，前后也不能误算两遍。应估计每区实际受伤比例。

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:43.560
For significant burn TBSA, include partial-thickness and deeper injury, not uncomplicated superficial redness. State which depths were counted.
重要烧伤TBSA应计部分皮层及更深损伤，不计单纯表浅红斑。应说明计入哪些深度。

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:55.176
Area is an estimate used with location, depth, age, inhalation and associated injury. It is neither a complete severity score nor an automatic fluid order.
面积是估计，需与部位、深度、年龄、吸入及伴随伤结合。它既不是完整严重度评分，也不是自动补液医嘱。

00:03:55.176 --> 00:04:04.920
A child is not an adult scaled down. The relative head and leg areas change with age, so adult nines can produce a misleading estimate.
儿童不是缩小成人。头及腿的相对面积随年龄变化，成人九分法可能造成误导估计。

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:15.792
The viewed local pediatric burn chart has separate age columns and a front and back map. Select the correct column and count the actual affected regions and depths.
已查看当地儿童烧伤表有不同年龄列及前后图。应选择正确列，计真实受累区域及深度。

00:04:15.792 --> 00:04:28.680
Do not take one region from a Lund-Browder-style chart and another from adult nines without reconciling their definitions. A hand region on a full chart is not the same as a one-percent palmar comparison.
不能从Lund-Browder类表取一区、再从成人九分法取另一区，却不核对定义。完整表上的手区，不等于1%掌面参照。

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:39.048
Communicate the method and uncertainty. An honest approximate area is more useful than a precise-looking number assembled from incompatible denominators.
应沟通方法及不确定。有依据的近似面积，比不相容分母拼出的精确外观数字更有用。

00:04:39.048 --> 00:04:49.008
For scattered small areas, the explicit reviewed palmar image uses the patient palm plus fingers as approximately one percent of total surface area.
零散小面积时，已核查明确掌面图采用患者手掌加手指，约占总体表面积1%。

00:04:49.008 --> 00:04:58.608
Use the patient hand reference, not the clinician hand. Small patches can then be compared without assuming every irregular wound is one complete hand.
应使用患者自己的手参照，不是临床人员的手。比较小斑块时，也不能认为每块不规则伤都等于一只完整手。

00:04:58.608 --> 00:05:10.992
The supplied Nancy text says palm excluding fingers equals one percent. That differs from the viewed explicit reference; do not silently treat the two as interchangeable.
所提供Nancy正文写不含手指的掌等于1%，这与已查看明确参照不同。不能悄悄把两者当可互换。

00:05:10.992 --> 00:05:19.992
State the method in the record and handover. A percentage is only interpretable when the receiver knows what surface and depth you included.
应在记录及交接中说明方法。接收方知道计入哪些表面及深度后，比例才有可解释意义。

00:05:19.992 --> 00:05:31.536
In our original adult example, the whole anterior trunk has partial-thickness injury, contributing eighteen percent. The entire right arm is also partial thickness, contributing nine.
原创成人例子中，整个前躯干为部分皮层伤，占18%；整条右上肢也为部分皮层伤，占9%。

00:05:31.536 --> 00:05:40.416
The left arm is red but has only uncomplicated superficial injury. It is not added to the significant-burn area in this calculation.
左上肢虽红，但仅有单纯表浅伤。本次重要烧伤面积计算不加入它。

00:05:40.416 --> 00:05:51.864
The included estimate is twenty-seven percent, not thirty-six. If only part of a listed region were burned, you would use that fraction rather than automatically the whole region.
因此计入估计为27%，不是36%。若某列区只伤一部分，应取相应比例，不能自动算整个区域。

00:05:51.864 --> 00:06:03.720
This is a teaching estimate, not an infusion prescription. The patient still needs airway assessment, source control, appropriate cooling, temperature protection and a destination plan.
这是教学估计，不是输液处方。患者仍需要气道评估、停止损伤源、适当冷却、温度保护及目的地方案。

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:14.712
Return to the patient whose voice is changing. Reassess the mouth, voice, secretions, breathing and mental state while maintaining the primary-survey priorities.
回到声音变化患者。应在维持初级评估优先时，复查口内、声音、分泌物、呼吸及意识。

00:06:14.712 --> 00:06:29.112
Hoarseness, soot, stridor or swelling can indicate an evolving problem. None by itself is an automatic independent intubation order, and the absence of a dramatic sign does not guarantee future safety.
嘶哑、煤烟、喘鸣或水肿可提示发展中问题。单一项目不是独立自动插管医嘱，没有夸张征象也不保证后续安全。

00:06:29.112 --> 00:06:41.760
Request the appropriate advanced airway team early when risk is significant. State how the airway is changing and what support is currently effective rather than waiting until access is impossible.
风险明显时，应及早请求适当高级气道团队。应说明气道如何变化、当前什么支持有效，不能等到完全无法接近才求助。

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:55.896
Protect oxygenation and ventilation within scope and reassess repeatedly. Do not delay effective support to prepare an unverified nebulized-humidity technique or copy an old airway category literally.
应在权限内保护氧合及通气，并反复复评。不能为准备未经核实雾化湿化技术而延误有效支持，也不能逐字照搬旧气道类别。

00:06:55.896 --> 00:07:08.496
Ask about the enclosed space, exposure duration, loss of consciousness, symptoms and other people affected. Toxic exposure can coexist with thermal airway or skin injury.
应问封闭空间、暴露时长、是否失去意识、症状及其他受影响者。毒性暴露可与热气道或皮肤伤并存。

00:07:08.496 --> 00:07:20.952
Conventional pulse oximetry can appear normal with carbon monoxide exposure. Point-of-care CO-oximetry also has limitations and is not a dependable stand-alone exclusion test.
CO暴露时，普通脉搏血氧可能看似正常。床旁CO共氧测定也有限制，不能可靠地独立排除。

00:07:20.952 --> 00:07:30.504
Other combustion toxins may contribute. Do not sniff for a remembered cyanide smell or use the absence of cherry-red skin as reassurance.
其他燃烧毒物也可能参与。不能去闻记忆中的氰化物气味，也不能因无樱桃红皮肤就放心。

00:07:30.504 --> 00:07:43.008
Use the indicated oxygen and consultation/conveyance pathway and communicate the exposure history. The patient condition and exposure matter more than a single normal display.
应采用有指征氧、咨询及转运路径，并沟通暴露病史。患者状态及暴露，比单个正常屏幕值更重要。

00:07:43.008 --> 00:07:56.400
Protect the crew and establish a safe treatment area before contact. Remove contaminated clothing and manage runoff so that neither another body region nor a rescuer receives secondary exposure.
接触前应保护团队并建立安全治疗区。应去污染衣并管理流液，避免其他部位或救援者二次暴露。

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:10.512
Safely remove suitable dry material before irrigation and identify the agent when possible. Do not attempt household acid-base neutralization or assume every water-reactive substance can be treated identically.
适合干物应在冲洗前安全去除，并尽可能识别化学品。不能用家用酸碱中和，也不能认为所有遇水反应物都能同样处理。

00:08:10.512 --> 00:08:27.960
Hydrofluoric acid can have systemic effects despite a small-looking wound. Do not follow the supplied textbook calcium-chloride-gel recipe; the reviewed CDC skin guidance explicitly excludes it. Obtain the appropriate specialist/authorized pathway.
氢氟酸即使伤口看似小，也可有全身影响。不能照做所提供教材氯化钙凝胶配方；已核查CDC皮肤指导明确排除。应取得适当专科及获准处理路径。

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:39.792
For chemical eye exposure, begin appropriate prompt irrigation without delaying for a complete visual examination, protect the other eye and continue reassessment and specialist care.
化学眼暴露应及时适当冲洗，不能等完整视力检查，且应保护另一眼，并持续复评及专科照护。

00:08:39.792 --> 00:08:52.656
Do not approach a downed wire or attached patient until qualified personnel confirm isolation. A line that appears inactive can re-energize; improvised attempts to move it can create another victim.
专业人员确认隔离前，不能接近落地电线或仍接触电源患者。看似不带电的线可重新通电，临时尝试移动可能再添伤者。

00:08:52.656 --> 00:09:06.168
Once safe, assess arrest, breathing and circulation and consider a fall, muscle contraction injury or other trauma. Begin indicated resuscitation and monitoring through the actual pathway.
安全后，应评估骤停、呼吸及循环，并考虑跌落、肌肉收缩伤或其他创伤。应按真实路径开始有指征复苏及监测。

00:09:06.168 --> 00:09:19.632
Small contact marks can conceal major deep-tissue injury. Reassess limb perfusion and neurological function and report the voltage/current history if known without pretending it quantifies the full injury.
小接触痕可隐藏重要深部损伤。应复查肢体灌注及神经功能，已知时报告电压电流病史，但不能假装它能量化全部损伤。

00:09:19.632 --> 00:09:32.616
Do not run fluid wide open simply to flush kidneys or assume every exposure needs the same monitoring duration. Use actual hypoperfusion, risk and the clinical/receiving pathway.
不能只为冲洗肾脏就液体全开，也不能认为所有暴露监测时长相同。应依据真实灌注不足、风险及临床或接收路径。

00:09:32.616 --> 00:09:44.208
Use the appropriate cool-water method to limit local thermal injury and provide pain relief. Ice or excessive cold can worsen tissue injury and whole-patient heat loss.
应采用适当凉水方法限制局部热伤并缓解疼痛。冰或过冷可加重组织伤及全身热丢失。

00:09:44.208 --> 00:09:54.576
Ask what effective cooling already occurred. The required total includes that time; do not restart a full course simply because the ambulance has arrived.
应问此前已做哪些有效冷却。所需总时间包括此前时间，不能只因救护车到达就重做完整一次。

00:09:54.576 --> 00:10:05.880
Protect the rest of the patient with insulation and an appropriate environment. Large areas, children and frail adults require particular attention to systemic chilling.
应以隔热及适当环境保护其余部分。大面积、儿童及衰弱成人，需要特别留意全身变冷。

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:16.296
After suitable cooling and decontamination, change to the appropriate covering and warming plan. Ongoing wet exposure is not automatically better care.
适当冷却及去污后，应转为适当覆盖及保暖方案。持续湿暴露，不自动代表照护更好。

00:10:16.296 --> 00:10:28.800
Current H10 says fifteen minutes of cool-water thermal-burn cooling. The saved assigned provincial guide says fifteen to twenty minutes. Both count effective prior bystander cooling.
当前H10规定热烧伤凉水冷却十五分钟，保存的指定省级指南为十五至二十分钟；两者都计旁观者此前有效冷却。

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:36.984
Keep the sources labelled instead of pretending the numbers are identical or combining them into a newly invented mandatory duration.
应保留来源标签，不能假装数字相同，也不能拼成新编强制时长。

00:10:36.984 --> 00:10:49.296
A patient with an immediate life threat needs the necessary treatment and conveyance. Do not delay solely to remain at running water; use the appropriate alternative while protecting the patient.
存在即时致命威胁者，需要必要治疗及转运。不能只为留在流动水旁而延误；应在保护患者前提下采用适当替代。

00:10:49.296 --> 00:11:01.512
For an actual school test, confirm the required revision. This lesson teaches the shared clinical purpose and makes the discrepancy explicit rather than supplying a false single official answer.
真实学校考试应确认要求版本。本课教授共同临床目的并明确差异，不能提供假的单一官方答案。

00:11:01.512 --> 00:11:14.592
After cooling and needed decontamination, cover with the appropriate sterile nonstick or dry material and keep the patient warm. Do not routinely break blisters or apply household creams.
冷却及必要去污后，应以适当无菌不粘或干材料覆盖，并保持患者温暖。不能常规破疱或涂家用乳膏。

00:11:14.592 --> 00:11:27.192
Assess pain even when a full-thickness centre is insensate. Use authorized analgesia and gentle handling, then repeat the same pain assessment and watch for adverse effects.
即使全层伤中央无感觉，也应评估疼痛。应使用获准镇痛及轻柔处理，再用同一疼痛方法复评，并观察不良反应。

00:11:27.192 --> 00:11:39.792
Circumferential deep injury and swelling may threaten distal circulation or chest expansion. Remove constricting jewellery when safe and reassess neurovascular and breathing findings.
环周深伤及水肿可能威胁远端循环或胸扩张。安全时应去束缚首饰，并复查神经血管及呼吸发现。

00:11:39.792 --> 00:11:52.368
Escharotomy is a distinct specialist intervention, not cutting taught as an independent PCP response. Recognize the concern, communicate it and expedite appropriate definitive care.
焦痂切开是专科干预，不是独立PCP切开处理。应识别关注、沟通并迅速推进适当确定性照护。

00:11:52.368 --> 00:12:03.096
Early hypotension in a burned patient requires a search for bleeding, toxic effects and other causes. Do not assume the visible burn explains every shock mechanism.
烧伤者早期低血压，需要寻找失血、毒性效应及其他病因。不能认为可见烧伤解释所有休克机制。

00:12:03.096 --> 00:12:15.984
A burn formula estimates a starting resuscitation plan over hours. Its clock begins at injury and its volumes need adjustment; it is not an amount to rapidly finish during a short ambulance trip.
烧伤公式估计数小时复苏起始方案。其计时从受伤开始，体积需要调整；它不是短途救护中要迅速完成的量。

00:12:15.984 --> 00:12:30.936
The textbook range, current adult burn-centre guidance and BCEHS license-specific instructions are different sources. Do not convert a CCP schedule or an adult formula into an independent pediatric or PCP bolus.
教材范围、当前成人烧伤中心指导及BCEHS分牌照指示，是不同来源。不能把CCP方案或成人公式变成独立儿童或PCP快速补液。

00:12:30.936 --> 00:12:47.592
Give only indicated care under the applicable pathway and reassess actual delivery and response. More edema, new respiratory difficulty or persistent poor perfusion means review the plan, not automatically finish a calculated maximum.
应只按适用路径提供有指征照护，并复查真实给入及反应。水肿增加、新呼吸困难或持续灌注不佳，需要重审方案，不能自动完成计算上限。

00:12:47.592 --> 00:13:00.144
Use the actual regional triage pathway. Current H10 includes large partial or full-thickness burns, smaller major thresholds in older adults and full-thickness injury above five percent.
应使用真实地区分流路径。当前H10包括大面积部分或全层伤、长者较低严重阈值，以及超过5%的全层伤。

00:13:00.144 --> 00:13:13.152
Critical locations and electrical, chemical or inhalation injury may require specialist care even when the skin area is small. A hand or airway problem is not made minor by a low percentage.
关键部位及电、化学或吸入伤，即使皮肤面积小，也可能需要专科照护。比例低不能使手或气道问题变轻。

00:13:13.152 --> 00:13:25.656
Associated trauma and the changing patient also influence destination and urgency. Do not use an older textbook major/minor table as if it were the current local transfer rule.
伴随创伤及患者变化，也影响目的地及紧急程度。不能把旧教材严重或轻微表，当作当前当地转院规则。

00:13:25.656 --> 00:13:38.400
Communicate the injury time, mechanism, airway concern, area/depth estimate, cooling already delivered and response. A useful pre-alert prepares care before arrival.
应沟通受伤时间、机制、气道关注、面积深度估计、已完成冷却及反应。有用提前通报能让到院前就开始准备。

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:51.384
Hypothermia means a core temperature below thirty-five degrees Celsius. Peripheral or field measurements may not represent core temperature accurately, so consider exposure and the clinical picture.
低体温指核心温度低于35摄氏度。外周或院前测量可能不能准确代表核心温度，因此应结合暴露及临床表现。

00:13:51.384 --> 00:14:05.592
The teaching pattern is mild around thirty-two to thirty-five, moderate around twenty-eight to thirty-two and severe below twenty-eight. Do not treat boundary numbers as a substitute for actual physiology or a measured core temperature.
教学模式约为32至35度轻度、28至32度中度、28度以下严重。不能以边界数字替代真实生理或实测核心温度。

00:14:05.592 --> 00:14:19.104
Shivering may diminish as the patient deteriorates; confusion, reduced responsiveness, slow breathing or bradycardia can be important. Absence of shivering is not proof that the patient is warm.
患者恶化时发抖可能减少；困惑、反应降低、呼吸慢或心动过缓都可重要。不发抖，不证明患者温暖。

00:14:19.104 --> 00:14:30.216
Consider an older person in a cold home, a wet trauma patient or someone with metabolic illness, not only a mountain rescue. Continue to look for the cause and concurrent injury.
不仅山地救援，还应考虑寒屋长者、湿冷伤者或代谢病患者。要继续寻找病因及并存损伤。

00:14:30.216 --> 00:14:42.024
Handle the hypothermic patient gently, prevent further exposure and replace wet coverings appropriately. Insulate beneath and above and use the treatment environment effectively.
应轻柔处理低体温患者，避免继续暴露，并适当更换湿覆盖。上下都要隔热，且有效利用治疗环境。

00:14:42.024 --> 00:14:55.080
Use the approved warming method without placing a hot pack directly on vulnerable skin. Continue airway, breathing, circulation and indicated glucose assessment rather than focusing only on a thermometer.
应使用批准复温方法，不能把热包直接放在脆弱皮肤。除温度计外，仍需继续气道、呼吸、循环及有指征血糖评估。

00:14:55.080 --> 00:15:08.832
The assigned provincial snapshot says no active rewarming below twenty-eight, while current I01 describes passive and active measures differently. Keep that difference visible rather than creating a blended rule.
指定省级快照称28度以下不主动复温，而当前I01对被动及主动措施表述不同。应显示差异，不能拼成混合规则。

00:15:08.832 --> 00:15:21.312
For patient care, confirm the applicable operational plan and seek clinical support where needed. A historical classroom temperature instruction is not automatically the whole current treatment pathway.
患者照护应确认适用操作方案，必要时取得临床支持。历史课堂温度指示，不自动等于完整当前治疗路径。

00:15:21.312 --> 00:15:34.680
In severe hypothermia, breathing and pulses may be very slow and difficult to detect. A hasty check can miss signs of life, but an unbounded delay is not an assessment strategy.
严重低体温时，呼吸及脉搏可能很慢且难以检测。仓促检查可能漏生命征象，但无限延误也不是评估策略。

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:48.264
I01 and the saved provincial page use thirty to forty-five seconds, while the current N02 hypothermia branch uses sixty. These are source-specific instructions, not numbers to average.
I01及保存省级页用三十至四十五秒，而当前N02低体温分支用六十秒。这些是特定来源指示，不能取平均。

00:15:48.264 --> 00:16:02.760
The special pathway also changes shock and destination planning and may involve advanced rewarming resources. Use the actual arrest guideline and clinical consultation rather than inventing an all-purpose cold arrest protocol.
特殊路径也改变电击及目的地计划，并可能涉及高级复温资源。应使用真实骤停指南及临床咨询，不能自编万能低温骤停协议。

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:15.840
The limited-shock snapshot is not a rule for every cold-feeling trauma patient or ordinary normothermic arrest. Later cardiac-resuscitation teaching covers the complete applicable team sequence.
限制电击的快照，不是所有摸着冷的伤者或普通正常体温骤停的规则。后续心脏复苏课会教授完整适用团队顺序。

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:26.856
A seventy-six-year-old in a very hot apartment is confused, weak and breathing rapidly. The skin is sweaty. This does not exclude serious heat illness.
一名76岁长者在很热公寓中，困惑、无力且呼吸快，皮肤出汗。这不能排除严重热病。

00:16:26.856 --> 00:16:35.184
Do not require dry skin or a peripheral device reading above forty before acting on a concerning environmental and neurological pattern.
不能要求皮肤干，或外周器械读数超过40度，才处理危险环境及神经模式。

00:16:35.184 --> 00:16:49.968
Assess airway, breathing, circulation, glucose when indicated and possible concurrent illness. Heat illness can coexist with infection, stroke, medicines or other causes of altered consciousness.
应评估气道、呼吸、循环、有指征血糖及可能并存病。热病可与感染、卒中、药物或其他意识改变病因共存。

00:16:49.968 --> 00:17:01.800
Move to an appropriate cooler treatment environment and start effective active cooling while arranging the care plan. Do not simply give water and leave a confused person in the same room.
应移至适当较凉治疗环境，并在安排照护时开始有效主动降温。不能只给水，就把困惑者留在原房间。

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:12.600
Environmental heat illness occurs when heat accumulation exceeds effective heat loss. It is not the same mechanism as an infection-related change in the temperature set point.
环境性热病发生于热积聚超过有效散热，机制不同于感染相关温度设定点改变。

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:25.512
Significant neurological dysfunction is especially concerning for heat stroke. A person may be sweating and still critically ill; skin appearance alone does not separate every exhaustion and stroke case.
明显神经功能异常特别提示热射病。患者可以出汗但仍危重，单凭皮肤不能区分所有热衰竭与热射病。

00:17:25.512 --> 00:17:37.536
Do not use antipyretics such as acetaminophen or aspirin to treat environmental heat stroke. The key intervention is rapid effective cooling with supportive care and appropriate conveyance.
不能用对乙酰氨基酚或阿司匹林等退热药治疗环境性热射病。关键是迅速有效降温、支持照护及适当转运。

00:17:37.536 --> 00:17:49.440
Investigate competing causes without withholding cooling from an appropriately suspected heat emergency. Repeated neurological and physiological assessment tests whether the plan is working.
应检查其他病因，但不能因此不给有依据疑似热急症降温。反复神经及生理评估，可检验方案是否有效。

00:17:49.440 --> 00:18:02.136
Begin the best available approved active-cooling method promptly and continue during conveyance when feasible. A cooler room or ambulance alone may be inadequate for a critically heat-injured patient.
应及时开始现有最佳批准主动降温方法，可行时在转运中继续。对危重热伤者，仅换到较凉房间或救护车可能不足。

00:18:02.136 --> 00:18:14.328
The assigned page includes wetting and convective airflow methods. Use an effective patient-specific plan; fans alone in very hot air are not a reliable heat-stroke treatment.
指定页包括湿润及对流气流方法。应采用有效个体方案；非常热空气中只吹风扇，不是可靠热射病治疗。

00:18:14.328 --> 00:18:28.224
Fluids address indicated dehydration or hypoperfusion and require reassessment. Oral fluid is unsuitable when consciousness or swallowing is unsafe and is not an effective primary cooling method.
液体处理有指征脱水或灌注不足，需复评。意识或吞咽不安全时不适合口服液体，而且口服液体不是有效主要降温方式。

00:18:28.224 --> 00:18:41.616
The snapshot ten-minute pre-conveyance wording must not postpone a necessary rescue or treatment of another immediate threat. Coordinate cooling, safe transfer, monitoring and early communication.
快照转运前十分钟措辞，不能推迟必要救援或处理另一即时威胁。应协调降温、安全转移、监测及早期沟通。

00:18:41.616 --> 00:18:54.816
The BCEHS guide below includes all eight named identifiers, not only the familiar tourniquet page. It connects recognition, intervention, reassessment and the license-level boundary.
下方BCEHS导读包括全部八项具名编号，不只熟悉的止血带页。它联系识别、干预、复评及牌照层级边界。

00:18:54.816 --> 00:19:07.344
The provincial guide includes the separated-part page, Sager examination sequence and image-only spinal diagram. A short topic label must not hide a listed reading requirement.
省级导读包括离断部分页、Sager考试顺序及仅图像脊柱图。简短主题标签不能隐藏列出的阅读要求。

00:19:07.344 --> 00:19:20.880
Nancy supplies the main-exam mechanism reading. It complements, rather than replaces, the named school books. The other Week Four textbook rows remain separate production work until their paired guides are added.
Nancy提供考试主教材机制阅读，是补充而不是替代学校具名教材。第4周其他教材行，仍是独立制作任务，直到加入各自中英导读。

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:34.416
For review, explain one original patient through the whole sequence and name an important source conflict. Memorizing a guideline code without understanding the patient does not meet the learning purpose.
复习时，应以一个原创患者解释整个顺序，并说出一项重要来源冲突。只背指南编号而不理解患者，不符合学习目的。

00:19:34.416 --> 00:19:46.080
At the burn station, identify the source, primary threats, included area and method. Explain what cooling already occurred and how you will avoid whole-patient chilling.
烧伤站应识别来源、初级威胁、计入面积及方法。应解释已完成哪些冷却，以及如何避免全身冷透。

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:57.384
At the cold station, demonstrate gentle movement and insulation, then identify the actual rewarming and arrest sources without merging their differing instructions.
低温站应展示轻柔移动及隔热，再指出真实复温及骤停来源，不把不同指示拼接。

00:19:57.384 --> 00:20:11.016
At the heat station, recognize neurological concern even with sweating, initiate effective cooling and reassess the patient. Explain why an antipyretic or a bottle of water alone is not the treatment.
热病站应在仍出汗时识别神经危险，开始有效降温并复评。应解释为何退热药或单一水瓶不是治疗。

00:20:11.016 --> 00:20:25.368
For each handover, give exposure and time, actual findings, interventions already delivered, response and what remains urgent. Keep estimates and suspected diagnoses clearly labelled.
每次交接都应给出暴露及时间、真实发现、已实施干预、反应及仍紧急问题。估计及疑似诊断应清楚标明。

00:20:25.368 --> 00:21:02.760
Read the four D02 hemorrhage classes as illustrative patterns, not measured blood loss. Class I is up to fifteen percent with little rate change and preserved pressure. Class II is fifteen to thirty percent: pulse around one hundred to one hundred twenty, breathing around twenty to twenty-four and a narrowing pulse pressure may precede a systolic fall. These are source teaching bands, not permission to wait for a percentage, a particular pulse or hypotension before controlling bleeding. Age, medicines, pain and injury can alter the expected pattern.
把D02四级失血读成示例模式，不是量出的失血量。I级为最多百分之十五，心率变化少且血压可保留；II级为百分之十五至三十，脉搏约100至120、呼吸约20至24及脉压变窄，可先于收缩压下降。这些是来源教学分段，不能等到某百分比、某脉搏或低血压才止血。年龄、药物、疼痛及损伤都可改变预期模式。

00:21:02.760 --> 00:21:48.024
Class III describes thirty to forty percent with hypotension and mental-status change; Class IV exceeds forty percent, with severe circulatory/mental depression and very low urine output. D02 flags systolic pressure below ninety or a fall of twenty-to-thirty percent from presentation as concerning. Its advanced column discusses blood components, calcium support and targeted anticoagulant reversal, not new PCP prescribing. The shared H01/D02 response is definitive bleeding control, appropriate destination and limiting hypothermia, acidosis and coagulopathy; a better pressure number is not replacement of lost blood.
III级描述百分之三十至四十，出现低血压及意识变化；IV级超过百分之四十，有严重循环和意识抑制、尿量极少。D02把收缩压低于90，或较初到时下降百分之二十至三十，列为警示。其高级人员段讨论血液成分、钙支持及针对性抗凝逆转，不新增PCP处方权。H01及D02共同方向是确定性止血、适当目的地，并限制低体温、酸中毒及凝血障碍；血压数字变好不等于已补回丢失血液。

00:21:48.024 --> 00:22:32.640
The actual PR03 placement reference is five-to-eight centimetres above the injury, or as high on the limb as possible, clear of joints and directly on skin. Its sequence uses a direct-pressure attempt followed by indicated device control, not repeated ineffective pressure while catastrophic bleeding continues. Remove slack, tighten the actual windlass device until bleeding stops, lock and record time, then reassess after movement. The two-hour statement triggers planning and consultation for delay, not scheduled loosening or automatic removal. Crush-related use is a separate consultation consideration, not routine prophylactic use for every trapped limb.
实际PR03定位参考为伤口上方五至八厘米，或肢体尽可能高处，避关节并直接贴皮肤。其流程为直接压迫尝试后，按指征用器材止血，不是在灾难性出血中反复无效压迫。应消除松弛，按真实绞棒器材收紧至出血停止、锁定并记时间，移动后复查。两小时条目用于延误时规划会诊，不是定时松开或自动取下。挤压伤相关使用另有会诊考虑，不是所有受困肢体常规预防性使用。

00:22:32.640 --> 00:23:14.376
In the PR02 T-POD example, expose the skin, position the belt at the greater trochanters, trim it to leave its specified fifteen-to-twenty-centimetre anterior gap, attach the tension system and draw it evenly to circumferential compression. Record application and any required or accidental release, maintain the closure and reassess. This is the named T-POD design, not an instruction to cut every commercial binder or a KED. Pelvic and isolated neck-of-femur injuries are not interchangeable; use the actual indication, device and trained movement method without repeated pelvic rocking.
PR02的T-POD例先暴露皮肤，在股骨大转子水平放带，按其设计修剪并留前方十五至二十厘米间隙，接张力系统，均匀形成环形压迫。须记放置及所需或意外松开时间，维持闭合并复评。这是具名T-POD设计，不能据此剪所有商业骨盆带或KED。骨盆伤与单纯股骨颈伤不能互换，须按真实指征、器材及受训移动方法，不能反复摇动骨盆。

00:23:14.376 --> 00:24:05.448
The H05 body defines full SMR as a collar, foam rolls without head tape and a clamshell through transport; it reserves clamshell conveyance for multi-trauma or new neurological impairment. The separate adult resource distinguishes simple and full approaches, not one board package for everyone. Assess cervical and thoracolumbar concerns separately, repeat motor/sensory findings and adapt protection to airway, breathing and positioning needs. The body states a pressure-above-one-hundred-twenty target with clear neurological deficit; the PCP bullet is broader, referring to suspected or confirmed spinal cord injury. Preserve both wordings and seek clinical support for competing hemorrhage, rather than silently narrowing the PCP text or averaging targets.
H05正文把完整SMR定义为颈托、不贴头的泡沫卷，以及全程蛤壳担架；蛤壳转运限多发创伤或新神经损害。独立成人资源区分简化与完整方式，不是所有人同一套背板。须分别查颈部和胸腰椎，重复运动感觉检查，并结合气道、呼吸及摆位需求调整保护。正文对明确神经缺损列收缩压高于120，PCP条目较广，写疑似或确认脊髓伤。须保留两种措辞；合并出血时求临床支持，不能暗中缩窄PCP原文或把目标取平均。

00:24:05.448 --> 00:24:46.728
I01 describes cold diuresis and ataxia in milder illness, then reduced shivering, slower physiology and declining awareness with worsening hypothermia. Afterdrop means core temperature can continue to fall during rescue as cold peripheral blood returns centrally. J or Osborn waves can occur after the QRS, but are not a stand-alone temperature measurement or a specific diagnosis. Keep movement gentle, prevent further heat loss and check concurrent causes including glucose, illness, trauma or intoxication. A stopped shiver or a warmer skin surface does not by itself prove core recovery.
I01描述较轻时可有冷性利尿和共济失调，恶化时发抖减少、生理变慢及意识下降。Afterdrop指救援中外周冷血回流，核心温度仍可能继续降。QRS后可见J波或Osborn波，但不能单独量核心温度或特异确诊。应轻柔移动、防继续失热，并查血糖、疾病、创伤或中毒等并存原因。停止发抖或皮肤变暖，都不单独证明核心已恢复。

00:24:46.728 --> 00:25:35.256
The I01 PCP reference considers warmed saline at thirty-seven to forty-two degrees Celsius for hypotension, thirty millilitres per kilogram with a two-litre maximum when available. That is its condition-specific source line, not routine fluid for every cold person, an exception to child cannulation limits or a way to combine every D03/BCPEG bolus figure. Assess breathing and perfusion throughout. Its arrest section considers an extracorporeal-rewarming destination within ninety minutes and recommends consultation when options are unclear. Use actual access, transport and special-arrest planning; do not infer that an unverified local service or a fixed travel time guarantees acceptance.
I01的PCP参考写可得时对低血压考虑37至42摄氏度温盐水，每公斤30毫升、最多两升。这是该病种来源条目，不是所有寒冷者常规补液，不取消儿童置管限制，也不能与D03或BCPEG各补液数字拼接。全程须评呼吸灌注。其骤停段考虑九十分钟内可达的体外复温目的地，选项不明时建议会诊。应作真实通路、转运及特殊骤停规划，不能以未核实的地方服务或固定车程保证接收。

00:25:35.256 --> 00:26:20.472
The January 2026 PR21 picture contrasts a BD twelve-gauge three-inch nonfenestrated catheter with a Turkel twelve-gauge three-and-a-half-inch fenestrated system. Turkel has a contact indicator and a stopcock initially closed; the actual opening step matters. The BD example does not require adding that stopcock. Control needle advancement at pleural entry, stabilize while withdrawing the sharp and advancing the flexible catheter, dispose of the sharp and reassess ventilation and hemodynamics. An air sound alone is not success. The source device pictures and adult sizing row are different references, not proof that every supplied adult device has one length.
2026年1月PR21图对比BD十二号三英寸无侧孔导管，与Turkel十二号三点五英寸有侧孔系统。Turkel有接触指示和初始关闭的三通，实际打开步骤很重要；BD例不要求另加该三通。到胸膜入口须控制针推进，稳住后退锐针、送软导管，安全弃锐器，再评通气和循环。听到气声并不等于成功。来源产品图和成人尺寸行是不同参考，不证明所有成人产品只有同一长度。

00:26:20.472 --> 00:27:08.976
The same dated PR21 table lists ages zero-to-four: twenty-two gauge, twenty-five millimetres; five-to-seventeen: eighteen gauge, forty-eight millimetres; eighteen-plus: twelve gauge, seventy-six millimetres. Treat these as source examples for authorized supervised teaching, not a universal child-device instruction or PCP authorization. The precautions include body habitus, term-pregnancy anatomy and mainstem intubation as a mimic of unilateral findings. Incorrect diagnosis or landmarks can cause a pneumothorax or other injury; blockage, kinking, displacement, bleeding and infection can follow. No absolute contraindication in a true emergency does not mean no indication is needed.
同一日期PR21表列零至四岁22G、25mm；五至十七岁18G、48mm；十八岁或以上12G、76mm。应作为获准督导教学中的来源例，不是儿童器材通用指令或PCP授权。警示包括体型、足月妊娠解剖，以及主支气管插管可模仿单侧表现。误诊或定位错误可造成气胸或其他伤害，也可有阻塞、折曲、移位、出血和感染。真实急症无绝对禁忌，不表示不需要适应证。

00:27:08.976 --> 00:28:01.968
Use the shock-drug interaction tables to obtain a real medication history, not to invent a new contraindication. The salbutamol table lists other sympathomimetics, epinephrine, MAO inhibitors, tricyclic antidepressants and beta blockers; the norepinephrine table also highlights MAO inhibitors, tricyclics and halogenated anesthetics. Their practical questions concern altered effect, rhythm, pressure and monitoring. A listed interaction is not a reason to replace indicated IM epinephrine with salbutamol, or to delay lifesaving anaphylaxis care. Verify the actual product and authorized plan. In a patient already receiving an advanced infusion, communicate the medicine, concentration, route, recent change, perfusion and line findings rather than taking over its prescription.
休克药相互作用表用于取得真实用药史，不能自行新增禁忌。沙丁胺醇表列其他拟交感药、肾上腺素、单胺氧化酶抑制剂、三环抗抑郁药及β阻断药；去甲肾上腺素表也强调单胺氧化酶抑制剂、三环药及卤代麻醉药。实用问题是药效、心律、血压及监测如何变化。列有相互作用，不表示可用沙丁胺醇替代有指征肌注肾上腺素，也不能因此延误过敏性休克救命照护。须核真实产品及获准方案。遇既有高级输注，应交代药名、浓度、途径、近期调整、灌注及通路所见，而不是接手开处方。

00:28:01.968 --> 00:28:51.936
Reconcile generic name, brand, formulation and indication separately. The skin table pairs hydrocortisone cream with Cortef, but the checked Canadian Cortef record is an oral tablet, not that cream. Its cantharidin row says Yanth and warts; the checked U.S. YCANTH label is a clinician-applied product for molluscum contagiosum in people aged two or older, not a universal wart instruction or proof of Canadian availability. Retapamulin is another topical antibacterial for selected impetigo treatment, while sodium sulfacetamide is a different antibacterial skin preparation with its own allergy/product precautions. These examples explain why one class or trade name cannot choose the route, lesion, age or treatment schedule.
须分别核通用名、品牌、剂型及指征。皮肤表把氢化可的松乳膏配Cortef，但已核加拿大Cortef记录是口服片，不是该乳膏。其斑蝥素行写Yanth及疣；已核美国YCANTH标签是由临床人员给两岁或以上者治疗传染性软疣的产品，不是所有疣通用指令，也不证明加拿大可得。瑞他莫林是某些脓疱疮治疗的另一外用抗菌药，磺胺醋酰钠则是另一类有自身过敏及产品注意事项的抗菌皮肤制剂。这些例说明不能靠一个类别或品牌，就决定途径、病灶、年龄及疗程。

00:28:51.936 --> 00:29:39.192
The literal final pages include summaries and key terms, and those shortcuts also need interpretation. Cardiac output is volume per minute, whereas stroke volume is per beat; the source definition that joins them is inconsistent. A dysrhythmia can be regular as well as irregular. Atrial fibrillation does not guarantee a rapid ventricular response. PEA means organized electrical activity without a clinically detectable pulse; it is not established just by saying that every muscle cell fails to respond. A vesicant can injure tissue outside an IV context too, as the cantharidin example shows. Use the clinical concept, not a mistaken one-line definition or a copied chapter-question answer.
字面末页含小结和术语，简写也须解释。心排量是每分钟体积，每搏量才是每搏体积；来源把二者接成同义定义并不一致。异常心律既可规则，也可不规则；房颤不保证心室反应必快。PEA指有组织电活动却无临床可探测脉搏，不能只说每个肌细胞都不反应就确定。发疱剂在非静脉情境也能伤组织，斑蝥素就是例子。应理解临床概念，不背错误一句话定义，也不抄章末题答案。

00:29:39.192 --> 00:30:26.352
Read the actual Parkland image as a hospital calculation, not a new ambulance order. Its first-day lactated-Ringer estimate is four millilitres times body weight in kilograms times the whole-number percent of included TBSA. Thirty percent is entered as thirty, not zero point three. Half of that estimated volume belongs to the first eight hours from injury and half to the following sixteen hours. The source also gives an adult urine-output benchmark above zero point five millilitres per kilogram per hour. That does not authorize catheterization or make urine output the only perfusion endpoint. Prior fluids, elapsed time, associated hemorrhage and clinical response must be reconciled by the responsible team.
把实际Parkland图读成医院计算，不是新救护车医嘱。其首日乳酸林格液估量为四毫升乘体重公斤数，再乘计入TBSA的整数百分数。百分之三十填30，不是0.3。估量一半分配于受伤起首八小时，另一半于随后十六小时。来源另给成人尿量高于每公斤每小时0.5毫升的参考；这不授权置尿管，也不使尿量成为唯一灌注终点。既往液体、已过时间、并存失血及临床反应，均须由负责团队核算。

00:30:26.352 --> 00:31:11.064
Original paper example: seventy kilograms with thirty percent included TBSA gives four times seventy times thirty, or eight thousand four hundred millilitres estimated over twenty-four hours. Half is four thousand two hundred. If the exercise starts at the injury time with no previous fluid, the two arithmetic rates are five hundred twenty-five millilitres per hour over the first eight hours and two hundred sixty-two point five over the next sixteen. The unequal rates follow unequal time blocks; do not divide the total by twenty-four and call that the first-phase rate. A delayed arrival changes the time accounting, not permission to force a catch-up volume or deliver the whole total as a bolus.
原创纸上例：70公斤、计入面积30%，四乘70乘30，得到首24小时估量8400毫升；一半4200。若题设从受伤时起且此前未补液，首八小时算术速度为每小时525毫升，后十六小时每小时262.5毫升。速度不同来自时段长度不同，不能总量除24就当首阶段速度。延迟到达会改变时间核算，但不允许强行追补欠量或把总量一次推完。

00:31:11.064 --> 00:31:54.720
Keep source versions separate. The school-copy image teaches the four-millilitre Parkland model. The published 2024 American Burn Association guideline recommends an initial two-millilitre-per-kilogram-per-percent approach to reduce resuscitation volumes in its defined adult group with burns of at least twenty percent TBSA. That is a specialist burn-resuscitation comparison, not proof that the school image was changed, a universal child formula or a replacement BC PCP order. Both under-resuscitation and excessive fluid can harm. State the model requested in an educational calculation, then use the actual local protocol, consultation and titrated clinical plan in practice.
须分开来源版本。学校副本图教四毫升Parkland模型；已发表2024年American Burn Association指南，对其限定的成人至少20% TBSA烧伤群体，建议以每公斤每百分面积两毫升起始，以减少复苏液量。这是专科烧伤复苏比较，不证明学校图已改，不是通用儿童公式，也不取代卑诗PCP医嘱。复苏不足与过量液体均可伤害。学习计算应先说明题目要求的模型，实操则依真实地方流程、咨询及临床滴定方案。

00:31:54.720 --> 00:32:49.464
Interpret the actual oxygen-device table by interface and response, not a fixed oxygen-per-litre rule. Its examples list a nasal cannula at one-to-six litres per minute with an approximate twenty-four-to-forty-four percent, a simple mask at six-to-ten with twenty-eight-to-fifty percent, and a reservoir non-rebreather at ten-to-fifteen with sixty-to-eighty percent. These are textbook estimates, not measured guarantees or one setting for every patient. Reservoir inflation, mask seal, inspiratory demand and device design matter. High-flow nasal systems, CPAP and a ventilator are distinct technologies. A bag-mask needs an appropriate gas supply, reservoir, seal and effective breaths; fifteen litres does not automatically establish one hundred percent inspired oxygen or adequate ventilation.
把实际氧器械表按界面及反应读，不能用每升固定氧浓度规则。表例鼻导管每分钟一至六升，约24%至44%；普通面罩六至十升，约28%至50%；储气无重复吸入面罩十至十五升，约60%至80%。这是教材估值，不是实测保证，也不是人人同一设定。储气袋充盈、面罩密封、吸气需求及器械设计都重要。高流量鼻系统、CPAP及呼吸机是不同技术。球囊面罩需适当气源、储气、密封及有效呼吸；十五升不自动证明吸入100%氧或通气足够。

00:32:49.464 --> 00:33:35.256
The actual heart-listening image maps sound windows, not the anatomical valve positions. In the usual adult surface map, aortic is at the second right intercostal space near the sternum, pulmonic at the second left, Erb's point at the third left, tricuspid near the lower left sternal border and mitral near the fifth left intercostal space at the midclavicular line. Compare sounds systematically with the clinical context; body habitus and anatomy can alter access. S1 mainly accompanies atrioventricular-valve closure and S2 semilunar-valve closure. These listening points do not replace rhythm, breathing and perfusion assessment or prove a valve diagnosis from one sound.
实际心音图标的是听诊窗口，不是瓣膜解剖位置。通常成人体表图中，主动脉区在胸骨旁右第二肋间，肺动脉区在左第二肋间，Erb点在左第三肋间，三尖瓣区近左胸骨下缘，二尖瓣区近左第五肋间锁骨中线。应系统比较并结合临床，体型解剖可改变可及性。S1主要伴房室瓣关闭，S2伴半月瓣关闭。这些位置不能替代心律、呼吸灌注评估，也不能靠一次声音证明瓣膜诊断。

00:33:35.256 --> 00:33:47.088
You should now distinguish cooling a thermal injury from warming a cold patient and rapidly cooling environmental heat illness. The same intervention can help one problem and harm another.
你现在应能区分热伤局部冷却、低温患者复温及环境性热病迅速降温。同一干预可帮助一个问题，却伤害另一个。

00:33:47.088 --> 00:33:58.368
Estimate burn depth and area with the correct age and reference, recognize inhalation or electrical/chemical risk and avoid formula-driven over-resuscitation.
应按正确年龄及参照估计烧伤深度和面积，识别吸入、电或化学风险，并避免公式驱动过度复苏。

00:33:58.368 --> 00:34:11.136
Use the three paired guides to retrieve mechanisms and all assigned protocol pages. Keep source versions and clinical authority visible rather than inventing a single blended official rule.
应以三份中英导读主动提取机制及所有指定协议页。保留来源版本及临床权限，不能编造单一混合官方规则。

00:34:11.136 --> 00:34:23.520
Complete the original checks aloud, then rehearse the station and handover with an appropriate partner or instructor. Reading completion is preparation for performance, not proof of a passed skill.
应口头完成原创自查，再与适当搭档或教师演练训练站及交接。完成阅读是表现准备，不是技能通过证明。
